## Technical Considerations

### File Handling for Remote Execution

When UI runs locally but pipeline runs remotely:

1. **Upload Strategy:** 
   - Large audio files uploaded via chunked upload
   - Progress indicator during upload
   - Resume capability for interrupted uploads

2. **Audio Streaming:**
   - Audio files cached locally after first download
   - Stream from server if not cached
   - Consider WebRTC for low-latency streaming

3. **Transcript Sync:**
   - Transcripts are small, fetch on demand
   - Local caching with ETag/Last-Modified
   - Edits saved to server, synced bidirectionally

### Security Considerations

1. **Authentication:** 
   - Start with simple token-based auth

2. **Data Protection:**
   - HTTPS required for remote connections
   - Audio files contain sensitive interview data
   - Consider at-rest encryption for server storage

3. **Input Validation:**
   - Sanitize all user inputs
   - Validate file types on upload
   - Rate limiting on API endpoints

### Performance Targets

| Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|
| Initial page load | < 2 seconds |
| Audio seek latency | < 100ms |
| Word highlight update | < 50ms |
| Save operation | < 500ms |
| Export generation | < 5 seconds |
| Support transcript size | Up to 100,000 words |

### Browser Support

| Browser | Minimum Version |
|---------|-----------------|
| Chrome | 90+ |
| Firefox | 88+ |
| Safari | 14+ |
| Edge | 90+ |

### Development Stack Summary

| Layer | Technology | Rationale |
|-------|------------|-----------|
| Frontend | React + TypeScript | Best for interactive editing |
| UI Components | shadcn/ui or Radix | Accessible, customizable |
| Audio | wavesurfer.js | Waveform + precise sync |
| State Management | Zustand | Simple, performant |
| Backend | FastAPI | Async, modern Python |
| Real-time | SSE (progress), WebSocket (future collab) | Right tool for each job |
| Database | SQLite | Embedded, no server needed |
| File Storage | Local filesystem | Simple, portable |

