## Appendix C: Mode-Specific Considerations

The pipeline supports multiple modes. The web interface must handle all of them:

| Mode | Audio Input | Key Differences |
|------|-------------|-----------------|
| `combined_audio` | Single file, both speakers | Requires diarization stage |
| `split_audio` | Separate files per speaker | No diarization, speakers known |
| `vad_split_audio` | Separate files per speaker | VAD-first pipeline, different turn structure |
| `single_speaker_audio` | Single speaker file | No diarization, simplified output |

**UI Implications:**
- Mode selection affects which stages are shown
- `vad_split_audio` has block-level (not word-level) timing
- Audio player must handle dual-track sync for split modes

